---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// Update this whenever the policy actually changes.
const lastUpdated = "1 June 2026";

const prose =
  "mx-auto max-w-2xl text-base/8 text-mauve-700 dark:text-mauve-400 " +
  "[&>h2]:font-display [&>h2]:mt-10 [&>h2]:mb-3 [&>h2]:text-xl/8 [&>h2]:font-medium [&>h2]:tracking-tight [&>h2]:text-mauve-950 dark:[&>h2]:text-white " +
  "[&>p]:mt-4 [&>ul]:mt-4 [&>ul]:list-disc [&>ul]:space-y-2 [&>ul]:pl-6 [&>ul]:marker:text-mauve-400 " +
  "[&_a]:font-medium [&_a]:text-mauve-950 [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-4 dark:[&_a]:text-white " +
  "[&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-mauve-950 dark:[&_strong]:text-white";
---

<Layout
  title="batze — Privacy"
  description="How batze handles your data: when you self-host, it stays on your server. This site collects very little."
>
  <section id="document" class="py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-2xl flex-col gap-10 px-6 sm:gap-16 md:max-w-3xl lg:max-w-7xl lg:px-10">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6">
        <h1 class="font-display max-w-4xl text-center text-5xl/12 font-medium tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-[3.5rem]/14 text-mauve-950 dark:text-white">Privacy</h1>
        <div class="flex max-w-xl flex-col gap-4 text-center text-lg/8 text-mauve-700 dark:text-mauve-400">
          <p>Last updated {lastUpdated}.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class={prose}>
        <p>
          batze is open source and built to be <strong>self-hosted</strong>. That shapes everything below: most of the
          time, your data isn't ours to handle at all. This page explains the little we do collect through this
          website, and how the batze software treats your data.
        </p>

        <h2>Your data in batze</h2>
        <p>
          When you self-host batze, everything you put into it — invoices, clients, projects, and email — lives
          <strong>entirely on your own server</strong>. We never receive it, see it, or store it. You're in control of
          that data, where it's hosted, and how it's protected.
        </p>

        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>This marketing site is intentionally light on data collection:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>No accounts, and no tracking or advertising cookies.</li>
          <li>No third-party analytics following you around.</li>
          <li>Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs (such as IP addresses) to operate and protect the site.</li>
          <li>The site loads web fonts from Google Fonts, which may receive your IP address when a page loads.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The demo</h2>
        <p>
          If you try a hosted demo of batze, treat it as a sandbox: anything you enter is for testing only, may be
          visible to others, and can be reset or deleted at any time. Please don't put real client data into the demo.
        </p>

        <h2>batze Cloud</h2>
        <p>
          A fully managed <strong>batze Cloud</strong> is on the way. When it launches it will handle data on your
          behalf, and this policy will be updated to cover exactly how — before you're asked to put anything real into
          it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy as batze grows. When we do, we'll change the "last updated" date at the top of this
          page.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy? Since batze is built in the open, the best place to reach us is by opening an issue
          on the <a href="#">project's GitHub repository</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
